    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36538" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑξᾰ-ετής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, or
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑξᾰ-έτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>six years old,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				3.1336
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				983.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				19.9.1
			</span></i>, etc.:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑξᾰ-έτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				14.33
			</span></i> (v.l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>of six years,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pyrrh.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑξάετες</span>”
				<i>for six years,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.115
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑξέτης.</span></div>
